it's tough to talk about the world of  cyberpunk without spending some time on  one of the major security corporations  of the future  militech if you've been following  gamespot's cyberpunk lore series you've  probably heard us talk about the weapons  manufacturer often  you may know militech as arasaka's  number one competitor but the  corporation's history runs much deeper  than that  [Music]  [Applause]  in 1998 the united states government  decided it was finally time to retire  the m16a2 assault rifle  marine corps officials were shipped a  handful of rifles to test out however  only three made it to the final trial  fn's sap colts ar-17x  and a firearm from a small weapons firm  called armatek lucey international the  sap was a cheap unreliable firearm its  only saving grace apart from being dirt  cheap was that the parts and ammunition  were compatible with the nato alliance  armaments  the ar-17x was an excellent gun with a  big  price tag although it passed the field  test with flying colors the united  states ultimately didn't think it was  worth the price  the weapon from armatech lucey  international proved to be the best of  both  worlds it was reliable and moderately  priced united states marine corps  general donald lundy a name you'll want  to remember took a liking to the  armatech lucey firearm  it was his number one choice however due  to the financial collapse at the time  the government settled on the sap and  drafted up a contract with fn  lundy unhappy with the government's  decision warned officials that putting  the sap in the hands of soldiers could  be disastrous  it turned out lundy was right thousands  of soldiers armed with the clunky sap  rifles died in south and central america  to make matters worse the european  community kicked the sap to the curb in  favor of the fnral  a fantastic weapon that was incompatible  with fn's sap  frustrated lundy left the marine corps  to work with armatech lucey  international  with his connections and experience he  was brought on as the acting ceo while  the founder antonio lukesi focused on  designing and creating weapons  thanks to lundy's connections to the  military he had no trouble securing  government contracts for armatech  lukkesi  these contracts gave the small arms  company a leg up over the competition  as armatech lucey international expanded  lundy and lucey decided it was time to  rebrand  and so militech was born militech's  first big break was to replace all the  saps the united states military bought  only a few years ago  i'm sure lundy walked into the pentagon  that day with a big old i told you so  grin on his face  militech's ronin light assault rifle  replaced fn's sap  and with that militech's popularity  skyrocketed worldwide  as militech grew and grew it swallowed  up smaller security corporations  soon competitors of all shapes and sizes  were being dismantled and absorbed by  the monstrous corporation  of course the lucrative government  contracts weren't the only thing making  militech a fortune many of their weapons  were sold and distributed to gang  members mercenaries everyday joes and  security departments and other companies  along with selling weapons and equipment  militech was known for hiring out their  private  military to anyone or anything with the  money to pay for it this includes but is  not limited to  assassinations revolutions civil wars  and according to the cyberpunk 2077  world book  ethnic cleansings yikes by 2020 militech  was the biggest weapons company in the  world  selling more firearms than any of their  competitors arasaka included  however money isn't everything and lundy  knew this militech's influence in reach  didn't quite match the arasaka family  and so a not so friendly rivalry between  arasaka and militech  came to be the rivalry came to a head  during the fourth corporate war  fighting between arasaka and militech  broke out all around the world in nearly  every major country  if you'd like to know more about this  conflict check out our video on the  fourth corporate war  in the meantime here are some important  bits arasaka and militech aligned with  nautical tech companies vying for market  control  early on arasaka and militech launched a  clandestine war against each other known  as the shadow war  eventually tensions bubbled over and the  two corporations kicked off a  full-fledged corporate-backed war  fighting persisted until a mysterious  pocket duke erupted in arasaka's night  city headquarters killing half a million  people  in response the acting president  nationalized militech and kicked arasaka  out of the united states  on paper militech won arasaka's reach  was reigned in significantly giving  militech an  opportunity to dominate the market  however militech's victory came at the  cost of their independence  president elizabeth cress had no plans  to surrender the corporation  after the fighting had stopped instead  she used militech's strength and  resources in an attempt to reunify the  united states if she was met with any  resistance she'd deploy militech troops  her regime wasn't entirely successful  many defected states including the free  state of northern california opposed  cress's campaign  ultimately crest slowed down on a  reunification plan as militech started  to regain its independence  however this wasn't the last time  militech got roped into a unification  war on behalf of the united states  government  let's skip ahead to 2069 recently  elected president rosalind myers  declared war on the free states of the  united states  many states were able to avoid fighting  or remain neutral by striking deals with  the federal government of the new united  states however the free states in need  of support looked to the mending arasaka  corporation with the devastation of the  fourth corporate war still somewhat  fresh president myers drafted up a  treaty and the war was put to bed  currently not much is known about  militech's presence in 2077.  according to the cyberpunk 2077 world  book the united states government still  has some control over militech but not  to the same extent as it did before  i have no doubt that militech will play  a big role in 2077 but i'm curious to  see how v  story may get intertwined with the  massive corporation especially if you  pick the corpo life path  if you'd like to learn more about  cyberpunk's lore check out our other  videos including one on militech's rival  arasaka and the deadly cyborg atom  smasher and with that we'll see you next  week  [Music]  you
 

